{"_id":"APOFj001Overview","name":"Prospero's Dream - Overview","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp001Overvw","name":"Station Overview","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Prospero's Dream</h2><p><strong>Population (City Level):</strong> 5.6 million</p><p><strong>Population (Choke):</strong> 3.1 million</p><p><strong>Ships Currently Docked:</strong> 1d100[+]</p><p><strong>Diameter:</strong> 12.98km</p><p><strong>Circumference:</strong> 40.77km</p><p><strong>Decks (Outer Ring):</strong> 23</p><p><strong>Decks (Ring Structures Avg.):</strong> 78</p><p><strong>Decks (Center Spire):</strong> 430</p><h3>What Is This Place?</h3><p>Prospero's Dream is a massive space station with a population of over 8 million. It's haphazard, disorganized, overcrowded, and teeming with hustlers and criminals of all stripes.</p><p>The Dream is operated by the <strong>Golyanovo II Bratva</strong> (AKA the Novos, or \"Yandee's People\"), a powerful criminal syndicate headed by a meticulous (secret) android named Yandee, backed by the elite Tempest Mercenary Company. Together they sell the lucrative drug Sycorax, which is supplied by The Solarian Church and distributed by Teamsters Local 32819L.</p>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj002Basics","name":"The Basics - Rules & Fees","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp002Basics","name":"Station Rules","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>The Basics</h2><h3>How do you board the station?</h3><p>Ships of Class-III or lower can enter through the dry dock. Once inside, ships are attached and locked into the station via crane and stored in the stacks until ready for departure. Ships Class-IV or greater must be moored to the station's piers.</p><p>Every ship is required to have an up-to-date manifest which includes the captain, crew, and cargo. IDs are checked upon entry, and discrepancies can lead to invasive searches, an impounded vehicle, or arrest.</p><h3>What happens when the crew boards?</h3><p>Upon disembarking, crews are directed by a station android to a Clean Room, where a squad of hazmat clad brutes (a Q-Team) strip search and spray them with disinfectant (<strong>4 Stress</strong>).</p><p>After decontamination they are issued an <strong>O2 credstick</strong> which acts as wallet, passport, and locator aboard the station.</p><h3>Laws of The Dream</h3><ul><li>Have your O2 credstick on you at all times. Your movements are tracked.</li><li><strong>Contraband List:</strong> Laser cutters, explosives, signal jammers, contagious bioweapons, EMP tech.</li><li>You can keep non-hull piercing weapons, but other weapons must be stowed in a rented locker (1cr/day/weapon).</li><li>Don't enter unauthorized areas, particularly The Choke.</li></ul><h3>Fees & Costs</h3><table><tr><th>Item</th><th>Cost</th></tr><tr><td>Docking Fee</td><td>10kcr/week. Impounded vehicles fine: Ship Class x 1kcr per day.</td></tr><tr><td>Oxygen Tax</td><td>10cr/day/person. 50cr/day during major events.</td></tr><tr><td>Seller's License</td><td>2kcr. Allows selling goods aboard The Dream.</td></tr><tr><td>Weapon Locker</td><td>1cr/day/weapon. All hull-breachable weapons must be stored.</td></tr><tr><td>Bribe</td><td>Minor: 2d10x10cr. Major: 2d10x10kcr.</td></tr><tr><td>Refueling</td><td>1d5x normal costs. Re-roll monthly.</td></tr></table>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj003Strike","name":"Storyline - Impending Teamster Strike","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp003Strk1","name":"The Impending Teamster Strike","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>The Impending Teamster Strike</h2><p>Ex-pilot <strong>Reidmar</strong> runs Teamsters Local 32819L, which makes money largely by distributing the lucrative drug Sycorax for <strong>Yandee</strong>, Vor of the powerful criminal empire, the Golyanovo II Bratva. However, tensions between the two groups are at an all time high after a small fleet of Reidmar's freighters are held ransom by the rival <strong>Stratemeyer Syndicate</strong>.</p><p>Yandee won't pay ransom, and Local 32819L can't afford to hire Tempest Co. to rescue the hostages. If a solution isn't found, the Teamsters organize a general strike and steal what remains of the Sycorax for themselves.</p><h3>Phase 1</h3><ul><li>Reidmar's freighter fleet has been captured by the Stratemeyer Syndicate. He demands Yandee send in Tempest Co. to rescue them.</li><li>The Stratemeyer Syndicate sends footage of Teamster executions. Reidmar threatens a general strike if the ransom isn't paid.</li></ul><h3>Phase 2</h3><ul><li><strong>Strike!</strong> Teamsters walk off the job. No ships may leave or enter port. Tempest Co. is overworked. Crime is high. Fuel/repairs cost 5x normal.</li><li>Tempest Co. strikebreakers called in to arrest Union leaders. Scabs allow some ships to leave. Fuel/repairs: cost 2x normal.</li></ul><h3>Phase 3</h3><ul><li>Brutal violence breaks out. Teamsters fight back against roving gangs of Novo Droogs and Tempest Co. Operators. Massive looting and rioting.</li></ul>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj004Unrest","name":"Storyline - Unrest in The Choke","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp004Unrst","name":"Unrest in The Choke","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Unrest in The Choke</h2><p>Those who can't afford to pay the daily O2 tax are sent deep below the bowels of The Dream into <strong>The Choke</strong>, where oxygen is scarce and life is short. This brutal prison houses millions living in destitute squalor.</p><p>However, revolution is coming: <strong>Imogene Kane</strong> and her insurgent resistance, the <strong>Hunglungs</strong>, are planning to overthrow their Tempest Co. guards and retake The Dream in a bloody revolution. Terrorist attacks are becoming more frequent and Tempest Co. and the Novos are responding in kind.</p><h3>Phase 1</h3><ul><li>Footage of Hunglungs demanding all O2 debt in The Choke be paid off in 24hrs or bombings will commence.</li><li>Bombings occur in a random module (roll 1d10). 2d100 dead. Tempest Co. begins to \"Search & Seize\" citizens at random.</li></ul><h3>Phase 2</h3><ul><li>Ukko/Ukka unmasked as Doptown rebel sympathizer/patron. Standoff at The Farm between Tempest Co. and The Solarian Church.</li><li>The Choke is quarantined. No one allowed out for any reason. O2 debts doubled on all citizens of Doptown until leaders turn themselves in.</li></ul><h3>Phase 3</h3><ul><li>Citizens from Doptown overrun the guards at the Airlock. War erupts in the corridors. Tempest Co. Armored Troopers butcher civilians.</li></ul>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj005ACMD","name":"Storyline - ACMD Outbreak","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp005ACMD1","name":"ACMD Outbreak","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>ACMD Outbreak (Caliban's Awakening)</h2><p>Two decades ago, <strong>Dr. Emil Bancali</strong> brought his terminally ill daughter, <strong>Ariel</strong>, to The Dream in the hopes of curing her rare disease through bleeding-edge cybermod treatments. Unfortunately, the treatments didn't work, and Dr. Bancali resorted to inhumane experiments.</p><p>He inadvertently gave birth to an outbreak of a new disease: <strong>ACMD, Acute Cybernetic Mutagenetic Disorder</strong>, which infects individuals with cybermods, slowly transforming them into fully cybernetic beings that then merge to become one with a being called <strong>\"Caliban\"</strong>.</p><p>Bancali was the first to succumb to ACMD, and has merged with the station itself, and is in fact Caliban. As more people become infected, Caliban gains more power over the station.</p><h3>Phase 1</h3><ul><li>Body Saves against infection are at [+]. Reports of mysterious figure roaming the slickworlds. 2d10 die in strange Slickbay accident.</li><li>First Chokespawn caught on the station. Rumors that the ACMD plague comes through the air filters from The Choke.</li></ul><h3>Phase 2</h3><ul><li>Packs of Chokespawn roam the corridors. Body Saves against Infection normal. Q-teams extort newcomers. Sycorax scarce.</li><li>Every 24 hours a random location is taken over by Caliban. Husks and Chokespawn run rampant.</li></ul><h3>Phase 3</h3><ul><li>Every inch of The Dream begins to morph. Metallic eyes and faces appear. Corridors become giant throats. <strong>Caliban takes over.</strong></li></ul>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp005ACMD2","name":"Infection Rules","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Infection Checks</h2><p>Unless the ACMD outbreak is cured, crew may have to make <strong>Infection Checks</strong> when contacting other infected, puncturing a hazard suit in The Choke, etc.</p><p>To make an Infection Check, first make a <strong>Body Save</strong>. On failure the character becomes Infected, and their <strong>INFECTION LEVEL</strong> increases by 1 (see Infection Table). Once per day they may make a Body Save instead of Resting to reduce Infection by 1 (1d5 on a Critical Success). On failure the Infection increases by 1 (1d5 on a Critical Failure).</p><h3>Infection Table</h3><table><tr><th>Level</th><th>Effect</th></tr><tr><td>01</td><td>Weak immune system. All Body Saves at [-].</td></tr><tr><td>02</td><td>Once/day make a Body Save or go into a coughing fit for 1d5 rounds. Anyone within Close Range must make an Infection Check.</td></tr><tr><td>03</td><td>Fever and chills. Suffer 1d5 DMG per day.</td></tr><tr><td>04</td><td>Gain a random Mutation.</td></tr><tr><td>05</td><td>Frailty. All Strength and Speed Checks are at [-]. Gain Mutation.</td></tr><tr><td>06</td><td>Suffer 1d10 DMG per day. Endure a Random Malfunction.</td></tr><tr><td>07</td><td>Panic Check. [+] on Reaping Checks until cured. Gain Mutation.</td></tr><tr><td>08</td><td>Install 1 cybermod per week or gain 1d10 Stress. Gain Mutation.</td></tr><tr><td>09</td><td>Once/day make a Body Save or spew an infectious Nanoswarm. All in Close Range must make an Infection Check at [-]. Gain Mutation.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Lose control of the character and transform into Chokespawn.</td></tr></table>","format":1},"sort":1,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj006DryDck","name":"01 - Dry Dock","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp006Dock1","name":"Dry Dock","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>01. Dry Dock</h2><p>Sparks fly as the harsh screeching of metal grinding fills the air and reverberates off the walls. Dozens of shipbuilders scurry around on scaffolding dangling above massive ships.</p><p>The Dry Dock is actually hundreds of small ports. This particular dock is only notable for being attached to Loshe's Office.</p><h3>Repair Costs</h3><ul><li><strong>MAJOR REPAIRS</strong> cost 2x as much as normal.</li><li><strong>UPGRADES</strong> cost 2x as much as normal.</li><li><strong>50% DOWN PAYMENT</strong> required.</li><li><strong>TURNAROUND</strong> time is 1d5x normal.</li><li><strong>10% chance</strong> some cargo is STOLEN.</li></ul><h3>Locations</h3><p><strong>1. CLEAN ROOM.</strong> Spartan, concrete room with rusty drains lining the floor. 1d5+1 Q-Team members wearing green hazard suits strip search and spray anyone who has disembarked with disinfectant foam guns.</p><p><strong>2. LOSHE'S OFFICE.</strong> Cramped, greasy office littered with tools. Loshe is usually here reviewing blueprints or negotiating a complex repair. A safe in the back contains plans for an experimental Jump-8 drive that requires only 4 Fuel to Jump.</p><p><strong>3. REPAIR BAY.</strong> Giant robotic limbs move independently, dismantling and upgrading ships. A few mechanics monitor the repairs.</p><p><strong>4. HANGAR BAY.</strong> This is where the crew's ship is docked during their stay. Guards can be hired from Tempest Co. Otherwise there's a 10% chance that some cargo is stolen.</p>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp006Dock2","name":"Loshe - Dockmaster","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Loshe - Dockmaster</h2><p><strong>COMBAT:</strong> 55 Exoskeleton Bash 4d10 DMG<br><strong>INSTINCT:</strong> 60<br><strong>WOUNDS:</strong> 3(40)</p><ul><li><strong>Exoskeleton:</strong> Four arms, each capable of attacking or firing a weapon in one round. Reapable. Worth 300kcr.</li></ul><p>Loshe personally oversees every ship that comes in. This makes him a hub of information about who's who aboard The Dream.</p><p>Speaks in a calm voice. Always smokes cigars. Drinks Cadre Cola. In recovery.</p><h3>What Does He Want?</h3><ul><li>To keep the dock running smoothly and without injury.</li><li>To get his 1 year sobriety chip.</li><li>To protect the Union. Despises corruption.</li></ul><h3>What Is He Up To Right Now? (1d10)</h3><ul><li><strong>1-4:</strong> Randomly inspecting a ship's cargo and manifest.</li><li><strong>5-7:</strong> Gossiping with the mechanics (Free rumor).</li><li><strong>8-9:</strong> Overseeing a Q-Team disinfecting a new crew.</li><li><strong>10:</strong> Meeting with Reidmar in the back office.</li></ul>","format":1},"sort":1,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp006Dock3","name":"Rumor Table","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Rumors (100cr per roll)</h2><table><tr><th>d10</th><th>Rumor</th></tr><tr><td>01</td><td>There's creatures growing in The Choke.</td></tr><tr><td>02</td><td>Yandee is secretly an android.</td></tr><tr><td>03</td><td>Cutter is looking to overthrow Yandee.</td></tr><tr><td>04</td><td>Ukko/Ukka is a Hunglung sympathizer.</td></tr><tr><td>05</td><td>Imogene Kane is planning an uprising.</td></tr><tr><td>06</td><td>Sycorax makes installing cybermods easy.</td></tr><tr><td>07</td><td>Angus knows everything about everyone.</td></tr><tr><td>08</td><td>Brunhildh keeps a pet monster in the cells.</td></tr><tr><td>09</td><td>Something called \"Caliban\" is infecting the terminals.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>The Aarnivalkea can heal any disease.</td></tr></table>","format":1},"sort":2,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj007Stllar","name":"02 - The Stellar Burn","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp007Stl1","name":"The Stellar Burn","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>02. The Stellar Burn</h2><p>Dark, smoky, filled with strobing lights and flashing lasers, The Stellar Burn is the place to unwind and do much of the station's \"business.\" Security is handled by Gundrones and Tempest Co. Probies.</p><h3>Locations</h3><p><strong>1. SEM'S BAR (CLUB LEVEL).</strong> Jury \"Sem\" Semenov runs the club level and is often found behind the bar. Sem dispenses a rumor if you've bought a drink. Any patrons going upstairs for a private booth need their retinas scanned (via a cybermod in Sem's palm) or the Gundrones are alerted.</p><p><strong>2. HEAVEN (UPPER LEVEL).</strong> Overlooks the bar and dance floor, and contains private booths with sonic muting.</p><p><strong>3. THE ECSTACY (LOWER LEVEL).</strong> Indyl's exclusive domain, where companionship can be bought. 100cr entry fee.</p><h3>Gundrone</h3><p><strong>COMBAT:</strong> 60 SMG 2d10 DMG<br><strong>INSTINCT:</strong> 25<br><strong>WOUNDS:</strong> 1(15)<br><strong>Special:</strong> Flying</p>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp007Stl2","name":"Menu - Sem's Bar","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>What's on the Menu?</h2><h3>Sem's Bar</h3><table><tr><th>Drink</th><th>Price</th></tr><tr><td><strong>CHATTER.</strong> Adzuki beans. Chat grubs. Corn.</td><td>15cr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>MOLOKO+.</strong> Milk. Synthemesc. Hallucinogen (Body Save or hallucinate, all rolls at [-] for 1d10 hours).</td><td>25cr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>AMBROSIA.</strong> Midori. Blue curacao. Lime juice.</td><td>20cr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>VICTORY GIN.</strong> Sickly. Oily smelling. Acidic.</td><td>12cr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>VESPER.</strong> Three measures gin to one measure vodka, half measure Lillet. Shaken. Lemon peel.</td><td>30cr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>CADRE COLA.</strong> Caffeinated cola beverage.</td><td>1cr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>SMOKEY.</strong> Mescal margarita. Dry.</td><td>15cr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>WELL DRINK.</strong> Blood Mary, Gin & Tonic, Long Island Iced Tea, Margarita, Rum & Coke, etc.</td><td>10cr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>CALL DRINK.</strong> Mixed drink with particular brand of liquor.</td><td>20-75cr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>BEER.</strong> Can or bottle.</td><td>5cr</td></tr></table><p><strong>BODY SAVES FOR DRUNKENNESS:</strong> Made at [+] after a few drinks, normal for a casual outing or [-] for a long night of heavy drinking. [-] to all rolls while drunk. Lasts 1d10 hours.</p><h3>Heaven</h3><ul><li><strong>SYCORAX.</strong> Neon pink pill. Strong sense of euphoria for cybermod users. 1kcr/pill.</li><li><strong>PRIVATE VIP BOOTH.</strong> Complete sonic muting and dynamic privacy tinting. 250cr.</li><li><strong>BALCONY ACCESS.</strong> Semi-private booths with a balcony view of the dance floor. 50cr.</li></ul><h3>The Ecstacy</h3><ul><li><strong>COVER CHARGE.</strong> Required payment to gain access. 100cr.</li><li><strong>PRIVATE DANCE.</strong> A dance in a private soundproof booth. Reduce 1d5 Stress [-]. 20cr.</li><li><strong>HOURLY RATE.</strong> An hour alone in a private room. Reduce 1d5 Stress [+]. 100cr.</li><li><strong>OVERNIGHT.</strong> Companionship for an evening out or in. Reduce 1d10 Stress. 1,500cr.</li><li><strong>XP SLICK.</strong> Recording of time with companion. 40cr/hr for your own. 5kcr/hr for someone else's.</li></ul>","format":1},"sort":1,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp007Stl3","name":"Indyl - Procurer","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Indyl - Procurer</h2><p><strong>COMBAT:</strong> 35 Retractable Nanoblade 2d10 DMG or Laser Pistol 1d100 DMG<br><strong>INSTINCT:</strong> 85<br><strong>WOUNDS:</strong> 5(15)</p><ul><li><strong>Pheromone Transmitter:</strong> Body Save or [-] to acting against Indyl.</li><li><strong>Poison Tongue:</strong> After a successful hit Indyl can use their tongue like a poisonous stinger. Body Save at [-] or be paralyzed for 1d10 hours.</li></ul><p>Runs The Ecstasy. Tall and graceful. Staunchly protective of their workers. Covered in esoteric motion-tattoos. Indyl's personal bodyguards, the <strong>Seraphs of Virtue</strong>, are highly skilled assassins with an 85% clearance rate who can be hired for 2mcr/target.</p><p><strong>MODS:</strong> Retractable Nanoblade (10kcr), Poison Tongue (400kcr), Pheromone Transmitter (2.5mcr).</p><h3>Seraphs of Virtue</h3><p><strong>COMBAT:</strong> 70 Electrified Lash 2d10 DMG or Smart Rifle 4d10 DMG (AA)<br><strong>INSTINCT:</strong> 65<br><strong>WOUNDS:</strong> 3(20)</p><ul><li><strong>Tactics:</strong> Ambush, retreat, repeat.</li><li><strong>Electrified Lash:</strong> Body Save or fall unconscious.</li></ul>","format":1},"sort":2,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj008ChpShp","name":"03 - The Chop Shop","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp008Chp1","name":"The Chop Shop","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>03. The Chop Shop</h2><p>The Chop Shop is overflowing with trash and grime, barely kept up by its hoarder/cybersurgeon proprietor, <strong>The Babushka</strong> and her holographic AI assistant in the form of a small child, <strong>Zhenya</strong>.</p><p>Appointments are made through Zhenya after a background check proves that the patient is on good terms with Yandee and her people (being on the outs with Tempest Co. or Local 32819L is okay).</p><h3>Locations</h3><p><strong>1. CRAMPED ENTRANCE.</strong> Loud squawks upon entry. The entrance is cluttered to the ceiling and on every conceivable perch rests a holopet (birds mostly). Zhenya makes himself known to anyone approaching and helps schedule an appointment. Reapers must enter through the back and will not be admitted. Hidden amongst the mess, three child-sized <strong>Augmented Toys</strong> [C:55 SMG+ 2d10 DMG + Frag Grenades I:20 W:2(10)] have been outfitted as killing machines.</p><p><strong>2. RECOVERY ROOM.</strong> Six dingy bunks where those who have just undergone augmentation can recover. The beds are empty except for one filled with a melted lump of horrific organic cybermods. Investigation reveals it to be a terribly mutated former human (Fear Save). Zhenya will tell you that this is becoming increasingly common. Something is infecting cybermods on The Dream. Use of the Recovery Room costs 100cr/day.</p><p><strong>3. SYCORAX STASH.</strong> Sycorax is the main anaesthetic The Babushka uses, and there is always 1d10 barrels of the stuff laying around, guarded by an Augmented Toy.</p><p><strong>4-7. OPERATING THEATERS.</strong> These rooms are nearly always occupied. The Babushka spends near 20 hours a day in surgery. Zhenya handles all the bedside manner and the <strong>Surgical Beds</strong> [C:65 Surgical Tools 3d10 DMG + Sycorax Gas I:40 W:2(20)] have been built from the ground up as highly effective (yet often terrifying) surgical assistants complete with \"chipper\" personality (Fear Save). Room 7 is kept quarantined to treat ACMD Infected patients.</p><p><strong>8. BABUSHKA'S ROOM.</strong> Cramped, single cot hovel. Little black book on upturned cardboard box shows a debt to Yandee, infinitely huge.</p><p><strong>9. CYBERMOD STORAGE & REAPER BARN.</strong> The back exit leads to a private tunnel that extends down into The Choke. Reapers who have made contact with The Babushka use this entrance to sell their reaped wares. There are 2d10 of each cybermod listed as well as anything else the Warden requires.</p>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp008Chp2","name":"The Babushka","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>The Babushka - Cybersurgeon</h2><p><strong>COMBAT:</strong> 25 Sawed-Off Combat Shotgun 2d10+2 DMG or MegaTranq Rifle 1d10 DMG and Body Save [-] or fall unconscious<br><strong>INSTINCT:</strong> 90<br><strong>WOUNDS:</strong> 2(45)</p><ul><li><strong>Cyber Savant:</strong> When she hits with any weapon, she can shut down any one of the target's cybermod for the duration of the encounter.</li></ul><p>Legendary cybersurgeon. Intensely private. Clinically removed from her patients, but generally has a good heart. Doesn't speak much, letting Zhenya, her holographic AI child, do most of the talking.</p><p><strong>MODS:</strong> Unknown. Assume everything.</p><p><strong>POSSESSIONS:</strong> Bag of useless junk.</p><h3>Jobs for The Babushka</h3><table><tr><th>1d10</th><th>Job</th><th>Pay</th></tr><tr><td>1-4</td><td>1d5 infected corpses. Bring them here for study. Don't get sick.</td><td>2kcr/ea.</td></tr><tr><td>5-6</td><td>Sycorax pickup from The Farm. Talk to Ukko/Ukka, no one else.</td><td>3kcr</td></tr><tr><td>7-8</td><td>House call. Mutated patient has mysteriously died in their home. Visit the scene and collect evidence. Don't get sick.</td><td>15kcr</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Rumors of a Dr. Bancali modding patients in The Choke. Visit Doptown and track him down. See if he knows what's going on with the ACMD outbreak.</td><td>Free cybermod</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Yandee has called The Babushka in for a meeting. Provide protection.</td><td>40kcr</td></tr></table>","format":1},"sort":1,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj009IceBx","name":"04 - The Ice Box","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp009Ice1","name":"The Ice Box","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>04. The Ice Box</h2><p><strong>THE ICE BOX</strong> is The Dream's slang term for its highly illegal Synthetic Sleeving Facility and Slickbay venue. <strong>Sleeves</strong> are vat-grown synthetic humans into which a user's memories can be installed, allowing them to experience life or live again in a new body.</p><h3>Locations</h3><p><strong>1. THE SLICKBAYS.</strong> Hundreds of human-sized pods (\"Slickbays\") where users can enter a virtual \"Slickworld\" for education, escape and pleasure. While logged into a Slickbay players can install slickware.</p><p>After 1 month of continuous Slickbay usage, any damage taken in the Slickworld applies to characters in real life as well. Likewise, if a character dies in a Slickworld under these circumstances, they must make a Death Check.</p><p><strong>2. THE RUNWAY.</strong> Minimalistic, surgically-lit fashion runway where sleeves are paraded and inspected before purchase. Because sleeving is illegal, access to The Runway is restricted to appointment only. Ask Angus or The Babushka for an invite.</p><p><strong>3. THE NEMO MACHINE.</strong> The legendarily outlawed Neural Monitoring Machine downloads a user's memories for future upload into a sleeve. Procedure takes 24 hours and requires a Sanity Save or the character forgets the last 1d10 days. Critical Failure results in a Panic Check and total amnesia.</p><p><strong>4. THE CRYOVATS.</strong> Enormous facility where sleeves are vat-grown from scratch. Giant cryovats with sleeves strung up by their spines as they grow, dangling like fruit. Sanity Save upon first viewing.</p><p><strong>5. THE STACKS.</strong> Data storage of remote uplinked sleeve backups as well as thousands of sleeves in cryostorage. Freezing cold, at danger for hypothermia without proper protection.</p>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp009Ice2","name":"Ice Box Services","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Ice Box Services</h2><table><tr><th>Service</th><th>Cost</th></tr><tr><td><strong>Reclamation Sleeve.</strong> Built by memory wiping prisoners. Re-roll stats. 10% chance of learning a random skill. 10% chance of gaining someone else's memories.</td><td>300kcr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Model-A Series Sleeve.</strong> Bulk issue. Ten different physical models (A1-A10). Reduce all Stats and Saves by 5. Heavily discriminated against.</td><td>500kcr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Atlas X Premium Sleeve.</strong> Custom designed. +5 Strength, Speed, and Body. Recovery only takes 48hrs.</td><td>3mcr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Narcissus-1 Sleeve.</strong> Luxury designed. All new Stats. Spend 240 points between Strength, Intellect, Combat and Speed. Recovery only takes 12hrs.</td><td>50mcr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Sleeve Backup.</strong> Download memories in the NeMo Machine. Takes 24 hours. Sanity Save or forget the last 1d10 days. Critical Failure results in a Panic Check and total amnesia.</td><td>50kcr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Sleeve Storage.</strong> Monthly storage fees.</td><td>500cr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Slickbay (1hr).</strong> Enough time to install a slick.</td><td>5cr/hr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Slickworld (1mo).</strong> DIY or join a Clan Server.</td><td>100cr</td></tr></table>","format":1},"sort":1,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj010Farm","name":"05 - The Farm","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp010Frm1","name":"The Farm","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>05. The Farm</h2><p>Run by the <strong>EVANGELICAL SOLARIAN CHURCH (ESC)</strong>, The Farm is both the principle grower of food on The Dream as well as an important holy site for the Solarians, with thousands of pilgrims making the journey each year to see <strong>The Aarnivalkea</strong> tree.</p><p>Additionally, The Farm is a major producer of drugs for the GOLYANOVO II BRATVA and the church's High Gardener, <strong>Ukko/Ukka</strong>, has a close relationship with Yandee as their single source for the cash-crop drug Sycorax.</p><h3>What do the Solarians Believe?</h3><p>The ESC (also known as Invictus Sol or The Dawn of the Unconquered Sun) is a polytheistic star-worshipping religion centered around the core belief that all energy in the universe comes from stars, and that sun god worship is the oldest human religion.</p><p>Anyone can become a member of Invictus Sol by accepting a bindi, burned into their skull, called a \"Sun Spot,\" and then growing and maintaining a small garden in their home.</p><h3>Locations</h3><p><strong>1. THE SANCTUARY.</strong> Grand sunlit chapel. From the Altar of Dawn Ukko/Ukka leads all who seek in guided mediations at \"dawn\" (0600hrs), \"high sun\" (1200hrs) and \"sundown\" (1800hrs).</p><p><strong>2. THE SUN MARKET.</strong> Bustling farmer's market. Vendor stalls for fruits, vegetables, drugs, arts & crafts, etc. Hundreds of shoppers on weekends.</p><p><strong>3. THE GARDENS.</strong> Silent meditation gardens. Walking paths, reflecting pools, artificial nature sounds.</p><p><strong>4. THE MONASTERY.</strong> Access restricted to the Solarian Gardener Monks of the ESC (about 40 currently there).</p><p><strong>5. THE DRUG LAB.</strong> Guarded by 2d10 Tempest Co. Operators. Drugs manufactured for Yandee and distributed by Local 32819L. Sycorax is packaged here but secretly manufactured at Farm Two.</p><p><strong>6. THE SEED VAULT.</strong> Cryogenic vault of thousands of seeds. Guarded by Tempest Co. Armored Troopers.</p><p><strong>7. THE SOLARIUM.</strong> Massive artificial sun room. Access restricted to Solarians (or those who make a 100cr donation). Reduce Stress by 1.</p><p><strong>8. FARM ONE.</strong> Immense zero-g hydroponic farm operated by Swarms of Cybernetic Drone Bees.</p><p><strong>9. THE TREE.</strong> The Aarnivalkea, the first tree grown on The Dream. Gargantuan. Lives on a small artificial island in the center of a giant man-made lake. Roots go down four stories. Restricted access to Solarian Gardener Monks or anyone who donates 5kcr.</p><p><strong>10. FARM TWO.</strong> Only rumored to exist. Restricted and hidden underwater entrance reached from The Tree. Sycorax is manufactured here and its formula is a highly guarded secret.</p>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj011Canyon","name":"06 - CANYONHEAVY.market","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp011Can1","name":"CANYONHEAVY.market","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>06. CANYONHEAVY.market</h2><p><strong>CANYONHEAVY.market</strong> is an intergalactic haven for hackers run by prodigy hacker <strong>Angus</strong> (a.k.a. Ang-Hause, @NG, angryhoss, AnGoose). CANYONHEAVY is effectively the intelligence apparatus of the Golyanovo II Bratva but is a renowned and feared information brokerage and hacking collective in its own right.</p><p>Access is restricted to vetted clients, first met in a private booth at The Stellar Burn.</p><h3>Locations</h3><p><strong>1. THE BATTLESTATIONS.</strong> Zero-G. Rough sphere workspace coated in multi-terminal workstations. Dozens of hollering Console-Cowboys [C:25 I:65 W:1] under-lit in neon-green kick-off and drift between the terminals, commentating the current Clan Game in slang incomprehensible to outsiders.</p><p><strong>2. THE CANYONHEAVY DATACACHE.</strong> Zero-G. A humming nest of servers and terminals with the atmosphere of a church. Encrypted and guarded by 1d10 Mercenaries loyal only to CANYONHEAVY [C:35 Pulse Rifle 3d10 DMG I:35 W:2]. If the datacache could be recovered and decrypted it would net you 1d5bcr and CANYONHEAVY as a powerful, lifelong enemy.</p><p><strong>3. SYSOPS.</strong> Zero-G. Planning room for major operations. Hidden behind an old-school whiteboard is a secret tunnel to The Stacks used to arrange meetings with high-value clients.</p><p><strong>4. ANGUS'S OFFICE.</strong> Zero-G. A cramped and dingy office crammed with blinking terminals, mechanical keyboards and discarded takeout boxes.</p>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp011Can2","name":"CANYONHEAVY Missions","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>CANYONHEAVY Missions</h2><table><tr><th>1d10</th><th>Mission</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Infiltrate Local 32819L. Gain membership. Find dirt on Reidmar. Foment insurrection. <strong>50kcr.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Infiltrate the Golyonovo II Bratva. Become a Droog for Yandee. Report secretly to Angus. <strong>25kcr.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Locate and break into \"Farm Two.\" Find the formula for Sycorax production at The Farm. <strong>30mcr.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Contact Imogene Kane. Rumored Doptown. <strong>10kcr.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Locate Dr. Bancali. Ask around in Doptown. <strong>100kcr.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Make contact with Hideo Kieslowski. Reclusive genius rumored to be hiding in a private Slickworld in The Ice Box for over a decade. Convince him to return to reality to help with the ACMD outbreak. <strong>350kcr.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Extract Anouk Falconetti. Currently held on Sublevel C. Escort her to Loshe. <strong>750kcr.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Relay slickware message to Goblin X. Currently held in a high security cell at The Court. <strong>150kcr.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Retrieve Brunhildh's terminal passcode. Small disc. Hidden inside her library near The Court. <strong>375kcr.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Deliver Dead Drop. Visit specified private booth in Heaven and hide package. Do not open. <strong>5kcr.</strong></td></tr></table>","format":1},"sort":1,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj012Court","name":"07 - The Court","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp012Crt1","name":"The Court","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>07. The Court</h2><p>Presided over by Chief Adjudicator <strong>Brunhild</strong> and her retinue of Executioners, The Court of Prospero is the only law on a lawless station.</p><p>Anyone found breaking one of the few written laws or many unwritten laws on The Dream are thrown into <strong>The Holding Cells</strong> to await trial by combat in <strong>The Cage</strong>. Anyone accused of a crime has the right to a representation via an <strong>\"Advocate\"</strong> if they can afford it (prices start at 5kcr). The winner goes free and the loser, if still alive, is sent to The Choke.</p><h3>Becoming an Advocate</h3><p>Submit a thumbscan contract with the Accused to The Court. A loss by submission or death in combat means the Advocate doesn't get paid and the Accused is sent to The Choke (if an Advocate dies in combat, however, their estate is still paid). Advocates can also act as \"Public Defenders\" who work for anyone who can't afford an Advocate (pays 5kcr/win).</p><h3>Becoming an Executioner</h3><p>Donate 15kcr to the Golyonovo II Bratva and win 10 Advocate bouts (unless otherwise arranged by a sponsor). Accusers always have the option to fight as Executioner against the person they accuse.</p><h3>Locations</h3><p><strong>1. THE COURT.</strong> Throngs of spectators, thick stench of body odor and smoke. Rampant side-betting. Fights.</p><ul><li>STADIUM SEATING: 25cr/ticket.</li><li>FLOOR SEATING: 500cr/ticket.</li><li>BOXED SEATS: 15kcr/box (holds 20).</li></ul><p><strong>2. THE CAGE.</strong> An elevated, revolving stage fenced in with electrified cage (Body Save or 1d10 DMG and lose an action) which dominates the center of The Court.</p><p><strong>3. THE BENCH.</strong> Balcony boxed seating reserved for Chief Adjudicator Brunhildh, her retinue, and the major power brokers on The Dream.</p><p><strong>4. HOLDING CELLS.</strong> Guarded by 1d10 Tempest Co. Probies. Most of these cells are occupied with O2 debtors. In one particular cell (Cell 4A) is the grotesquely musclebound <strong>Rage of Caliban</strong>.</p><p><strong>5. THE PIT.</strong> Musty animal odor. Its cages contain horrific beasts and other freaks. Heavily guarded by 1d10 Tempest Co. Armored Troopers.</p><p><strong>6. EXECUTIONERS' QUARTERS.</strong> Twelve spartan rooms, each with a small bunk and footlocker.</p><p><strong>7. ADJUDICATOR'S QUARTERS.</strong> Brunhildh's lavish suite decorated in old leather and hunting trophies. Hidden behind a bookcase is a secret alcove containing an android charging unit and private terminal.</p>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj013Tmpst","name":"08 - Tempest Company HQ","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp013Tmp1","name":"Tempest Company HQ","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>08. Tempest Company HQ</h2><p><strong>Tempest Mercenary Company</strong> is a detachment of the Czernobog Private Military Corporation. Their core mission is to act as muscle for the Golyanovo II Bratva. Led by <strong>Cmdr. Race Cutter</strong>, Tempest is primarily engaged in defending Reidmar's fleet during Sycorax distribution, quelling insurrection in The Choke and eliminating Yandee's enemies throughout the sector.</p><h3>Levels</h3><p><strong>Level 1 - Habitat.</strong> Heavily fortified entry control point. Badged visitors can access the client consultation offices and The Blue Rabbit, everywhere else is restricted to Rank 1 (R1) and above.</p><p><strong>Level 2 - Operations.</strong> Security checkpoints at the elevators. The nerve center of all operations. Extensive monitoring of citizens of The Dream.</p><p><strong>Level 3 - Commander's Mansion.</strong> Cutter's lavish penthouse. Guarded by The Zirnitra, an elite Armored Trooper unit. Personal terminal reveals evidence of disloyalty to Yandee.</p><p><strong>Sublevel A - Armament.</strong> Security clearance R2+. Massive stores of weaponry. Probies in Slickbay training.</p><p><strong>Sublevel B - Research & Development.</strong> R5+. ACMD research is heavily quarantined.</p><p><strong>Sublevel C - Containment.</strong> R7+. 30min. elevator. Freezing cold. Access to The Veins via hidden ducts. Supersoldier Sleeve storage.</p><h3>How to Join Tempest Co.?</h3><p>To become a member of Tempest Co. roll 1d10 [-] on the Tempest Co. Mission Table, complete the mission and donate all the credits earned back to the Company. Once that's done the character will become a Rank 1 (R1) Probie with full standing.</p><p>To continue to rank up they must successfully complete a number of missions equal to the next rank. Members must kick back 10% of all credits earned to the Company in dues.</p>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp013Tmp2","name":"Tempest Company Ranks","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Tempest Company Ranks</h2><table><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Description</th><th>Benefits</th></tr><tr><td>R0</td><td><strong>Recruit:</strong> Do 1 job and donate all the pay to Tempest Co.<br>C:20 Stun Baton 1d5 DMG I:20 W:1 L:20 Salary: 1kcr</td><td>None.</td></tr><tr><td>R1</td><td><strong>Probie:</strong> Assigned to a fireteam with an R6+ CO.<br>C:25 SMG 2d10 DMG I:25 W:2 L:35 Salary: 1.5kcr</td><td>Access to Mission Table at [-].</td></tr><tr><td>R2-R5</td><td><strong>Operator:</strong> Full fledged member of Tempest Co.<br>C:35 Pulse Rifle 3d10 DMG I:25 W:2 L:35 Salary: 2kcr</td><td>+100cr monthly salary per rank. Access to Mission Table.</td></tr><tr><td>R6-R7</td><td><strong>Squad Leader:</strong> Leader of 1 squad (2 fireteams of 5 Troopers each).<br>C:45 Combat Shotgun 4d10 DMG I:35 W:2 L:35 Salary: 3kcr</td><td>+1 Expert Skill. All Mercs hired gain +10 Loyalty.</td></tr><tr><td>R8-R9</td><td><strong>Armored Trooper:</strong> Elite drop soldiers and deep recon scouts.<br>C:65 GPMG 4d10 DMG I:45 DR:5 AP:13 W:3(20) L:40 Salary: 5kcr</td><td>Exosuit. +1 Expert Skill. Always in high demand.</td></tr><tr><td>R10</td><td><strong>Platoon Commander:</strong> Leader of 3 squads and a Troopship.<br>C:65 Revolver 1d10+1 DMG I:65 W:2 L:65 Salary: 6kcr</td><td>Command Skill. Hire Mercs at 75% off. Assign missions to R2 squads for profit.</td></tr></table>","format":1},"sort":1,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj014Doptwn","name":"09 - Doptown","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp014Dop1","name":"Doptown","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>09. Doptown</h2><p>Slang for \"de-oxygenated people's town,\" <strong>Doptown</strong> is a hellish slum filled to the brim with suffocating people imprisoned for oxygen debt and kept low by a system that oppresses and exploits them. <strong>Upon entering make a Fear Save or gain 1d10 Stress.</strong></p><p>It is a waking nightmare of overcrowded streets and quiet death as the doomed inhabitants, derogatorily called <strong>Chokers</strong> and <strong>Rebreathers</strong>, live out the remainder of their lives in relative silence, afraid of wasting any breath.</p><p><em>It would take 50.4bcr to pay off the O2 debt of everyone currently living in The Choke.</em></p><h3>Locations</h3><p><strong>1. THE \"AIRLOCK.\"</strong> A heavily armed gate flanked by two cement turret bunkers (which can withstand 200 DMG) and 1d10 Armored Troopers [C:65 GPMG 4d10 DMG + Frag Grenades I:45 DR:5 AP:13 W:3(20)]. The commanding officer is <strong>Colonel Antonio</strong>, a banal drone who carries out his orders with cold indifference.</p><p>You cannot get back into The Dream without a pass, and Doptownians who are aware that the players have one are willing to kill to get it.</p><p><strong>2. THE AUCTION.</strong> A silent market where Doptownians offer their services at cutthroat rates in order to afford to pay down their massively accumulating O2 debt. Assassins and hitmen offer up their services alongside cleaning crews and personal assistants.</p><p><strong>3. THE SLUMS.</strong> Sprawling and cramped, filled with the stench of death. O2 beggars line the streets. Robbery is rampant. Roll encounters every half hour.</p><p><strong>4. THE LOTTERY.</strong> Doptownians gather up discarded O2 tanks and distribute them based on lottery. One entry per person. If the players enter there is a 5% chance per person they receive an O2 tank with 1d10 hours worth of O2 in it. <strong>Imogene Kane</strong> is here, passing out O2 tanks stolen from The Dream.</p>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp014Dop2","name":"Doptown Encounters","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Doptown Encounters (1d10)</h2><table><tr><th>Roll</th><th>Encounter</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td><strong>Chokespawn:</strong> Running rampant and attacking Doptownians. Always stops to consume bodies.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><strong>Deceased O2 Beggar.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><strong>O2 Beggar:</strong> Cardboard sign of a clock showing how many hours the beggar has left to live. Those who don't donate must make a Sanity Save.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><strong>O2 Beggars, Family of Three:</strong> Child has a sign that says \"Paying for my father's sins.\" Those who don't donate must make a Sanity Save.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><strong>2d10 Beggars:</strong> Group of desperate beggars mob you for O2, credits, weapons, anything. Just anything.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><strong>1d10 Scavengers:</strong> Going from home to home collecting O2 tanks from the dead.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><strong>1d5 Tempest Armored Troopers:</strong> Patrolling. Harassing and murdering those who approach too closely.</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><strong>Standoff:</strong> 1d5 Tempest Armored Troopers and 2 Hunglung Snipers. Tempest mercs pinned down, calling for reinforcements.</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><strong>1d5 Hunglung Insurgency Recruiters:</strong> Want to take you to speak with Imogene Kane. They have snipers on you.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><strong>Imogene Kane:</strong> Leader of the Hunglungs. Has \"gills\" from Dr. Bancali. Seeking volunteers to infiltrate The Ice Box through Caliban's Heart.</td></tr></table>","format":1},"sort":1,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj015Choke","name":"10 - The Choke","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp015Chk1","name":"The Choke Overview","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>10. The Choke</h2><p>The Choke is a massive abandoned and quarantined wasteland deep below The Dream. It houses Doptown and extends into The Sink, a sunken city filled with horrors.</p><p><strong>All of The Choke is dark. The players need light to travel safely.</strong></p><p>It takes six hours to walk from one end of The Sink to the other and roughly a couple hours to get to any other connected location. Roll for encounters once per hour.</p><h3>Key Locations</h3><ul><li><strong>The Airlock (pg. 30):</strong> Gigantic locked gate to The Dream</li><li><strong>Doptown (pg. 30):</strong> Deoxygenated People's Town - a massive slum</li><li><strong>Life Support 01 (pg. 36):</strong> The sole remaining semi-functional life support system</li><li><strong>The Doctor (pg. 34):</strong> Dr. Bancali's hidden lab behind the sludge waterfall</li><li><strong>The Sink (pg. 34):</strong> Formerly a major functioning portion of The Dream, now a sunken city wasteland</li><li><strong>The Veins (pg. 35):</strong> A series of drainage pipes, ventilation shafts, and maintenance tunnels</li><li><strong>Mass Grave (pg. 35):</strong> A one-story-high pile of corpses</li><li><strong>The Burrows (pg. 37):</strong> A cluster of cybernetic veins - the only place to harvest Sycorax fruits</li><li><strong>Caliban's Heart (pg. 38):</strong> The awful, pulsating center of the Choke</li></ul>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp015Chk2","name":"The Sink","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>The Sink</h2><p><strong>THE SINK</strong> is what remains of the once bustling downtown center of The Dream. It now lies in ruins, covered in twisting ropes of cybernetic wires, creeping around every fallen building. The Sink is dark, foetid, and quiet. Behind every shadow lurks some hideous abomination.</p><p><strong>Make an Infection Check once per hour</strong> unless wearing a hazard suit, vaccsuit, or exosuit.</p><h3>Notable Landmarks</h3><p><strong>JUNO TOWER.</strong> Former corporate HQ on The Dream. 34 floors above the waste and 4 sunken below. Sadistic Tempest Co. Sniper [C:75 Smart Rifle 4d10 DMG (AA) I:55 W:2] perched near the top, picking off travelers for sport.</p><p><strong>THE METRO.</strong> Dark descent down three creaking stairwells into abandoned Metro tunnels. Power can be temporarily restored with a successful Jury Rigging or Engineering Check.</p><p><strong>THE OUTPOST.</strong> Tempest Co. Forward Operating Base in a crumbling apartment building. 1d5 Paranoid Operators [C:25 SMG 2d10 DMG I:25 W:2]</p><p><strong>THE SEWERS.</strong> Reached by spelunking down a 100' drop in the cracked pavement. Leads to the Mass Grave and The Burrows. Roll for encounters twice per hour.</p><p><strong>(HARD TO FIND) THE ARCHIVES.</strong> Decayed corporate research facility. Requires a guide or significant time spent to find. Investigation of patient records reveals that Dr. Bancali and his daughter Ariel came to The Dream 23 years ago to cure her terminal cancer.</p>","format":1},"sort":1,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp015Chk3","name":"Choke Encounters","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Choke Encounters (1d10)</h2><table><tr><th>Roll</th><th>Encounter</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td><strong>Discarded O2 tank.</strong> 1d10hrs remaining.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><strong>Septic Wave.</strong> Fear Save or be split up.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><strong>Sink hole.</strong> Body Save or fall to lower level. Take 1d10 DMG.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><strong>Doptownian</strong> looking for a place to die.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><strong>2d10 Hunglungs</strong> [C:25 Spears 1d10+1 DMG I:25 W:1] waiting in ambush.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><strong>1d10 Hunglung Engineers</strong> heading to Life Support 01, dragging a huge replacement filter. Without help, they won't survive the trip there.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><strong>1d5 Tempest Operators</strong> [C:35 Pulse Rifle 3d10 DMG I:25 W:2] lost and paranoid.</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><strong>Chokespawn.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><strong>1d10 Chokespawn.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><strong>The Wire Man:</strong> 10 story tall faceless behemoth built entirely of wires. Stomps reverberate across The Sink. Easy to hide from but he peers into cracks and broken windows. <strong>Massive Swipe:</strong> 1d100 DMG Body Save to avoid. <strong>Wounds 5(200).</strong> Retreats after gaining a Wound.</td></tr></table>","format":1},"sort":2,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj016Imprt","name":"Important People","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp016Imp1","name":"Golyanovo II Bratva","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>The Golyanovo II Bratva</h2><h3>Yandee - Vor of the Golyanovo II Bratva</h3><p><strong>C:</strong> 65 Laser Pistol 1d100 DMG | <strong>I:</strong> 80 | <strong>W:</strong> 4(55)</p><p>(Secretly) an android built from scraps on a prison world, Yandee rose through the ranks of the powerful Golyanovo II Bratva empire by discovering the lucrative Sycorax trade. Methodical.</p><h3>Angus - Sysadmin of CANYONHEAVY.market</h3><p><strong>C:</strong> 25 Revolver 1d10+1 DMG | <strong>I:</strong> 75 | <strong>W:</strong> 2(20)</p><p>Runs the sector's most powerful data brokerage firm and the intelligence arm of the Golyanovo II Bratva. Loyal to Yandee. Always has a lead on work for a 1d10kcr finder's fee. Chatty, manic voice.</p><h3>Reidmar - Union Rep of Teamster Local 32819L</h3><p><strong>C:</strong> 35 Spanner 2d10 DMG | <strong>I:</strong> 55 | <strong>W:</strong> 3(20)</p><p>Union loyalist, fluid expression of their gruff exterior and notoriously impatient. Legendary pilot. Distributes Yandee's Sycorax to fund Local 32819L's corporate lobbying. Rough voice.</p>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp016Imp2","name":"Station Power Brokers","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Station Power Brokers</h2><h3>Brunhildh - Chief Adjudicator of The Court</h3><p><strong>C:</strong> 70 Blunderbuss 6d10 DMG | <strong>I:</strong> 65 | <strong>W:</strong> 3(45)</p><p>Retired bounty hunter overseeing The Court. Yandee's fanatic right hand. Feared interrogator. Settled here for quality Big Switch and combat. Uses a modded antique blunderbuss (2mcr).</p><h3>Cutter - Commander of Tempest Company</h3><p><strong>C:</strong> 75 Pulse Rifle 3d10 DMG | <strong>I:</strong> 55 | <strong>W:</strong> 3(50)</p><p>Established his command as a privateer during the Corp Wars. Widely feared as a salt-the-earth tactician. Security arm of the Golyanovo II Bratva. Doesn't trust Yandee. Unrelenting voice.</p><h3>Ukko/Ukka - High Gardener of Invictus Sol</h3><p><strong>C:</strong> 20 Unarmed | <strong>I:</strong> 60 | <strong>W:</strong> 2(20)</p><p>Born in Doptown, Ukko/Ukka harvested Sycorax to pay off their birth debt. Joined the Solarians as a chemist, rose quickly to High Gardener. Donates massive O2 to The Choke. Coughs.</p>","format":1},"sort":1,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj017Drugs","name":"Drug Table","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp017Drug","name":"Drugs","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Drug Table</h2><table><tr><th>1d10</th><th>Drug, Effect & Comedown</th><th>Price</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td><strong>Method.</strong> Complete and total eidetic memory for 2d10min.</td><td>80cr</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><strong>Liquid Sword.</strong> [+] on Combat Checks for 1d5 turns. Take 2d10 DMG after.</td><td>200cr</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><strong>Daytona.</strong> Gain an extra action for 1d10 turns. Reduce Speed by 1d10 after.</td><td>150cr</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><strong>Triumph.</strong> Grants [+] on the next 1d10 rolls. 1d5 Stress. Permanently reduce Max Health by 1d5.</td><td>300cr</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><strong>Soma.</strong> Don't gain Stress for 1d10 hours. [-] on Speed Checks for the next 1d10 days. +1 Minimum Stress.</td><td>125cr</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><strong>Ruckus.</strong> +1d10 Strength. -1d10 Sanity.</td><td>100cr</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><strong>Seed.</strong> Gain a new Skill for 1d10 days. Lower a random Skill's bonus by 5. A Skill reduced below 0 is forgotten completely.</td><td>350cr</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><strong>Stimspice.</strong> Grants the ability to read target's mind for 1d10 minutes. Gain 1d5 Stress.</td><td>500cr</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><strong>Slug.</strong> Mentally visit a virtual world shared by everyone taking Slug at that exact moment. Last 1d10 hours. Sanity Save.</td><td>25cr</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><strong>Sycorax.</strong> Grants +20 to Body Saves when installing cybermods. Heals Xd10 DMG where X equals number of cybermod slots installed. Addictive with mutation risk.</td><td>750cr</td></tr></table><h3>Sycorax Details</h3><ul><li>Grants +20 to Body Saves made when installing cybermods.</li><li>Heals Xd10 DMG where X is equal to the number of slots of cybermods and slickware installed.</li><li>Every time you take Sycorax make a mark on your character sheet and roll a d10. If you roll equal to or lower than the number of Sycorax you have taken gain a random Mutation, then reset back to zero.</li><li>Addictive.</li></ul>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFj018Calib","name":"Caliban's Heart","pages":[{"_id":"APOFp018Cal1","name":"Caliban's Heart","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Caliban's Heart</h2><p><strong>CALIBAN'S HEART</strong> is a slick wet pit of cybernetic and organic fusion. Every inch of these twisting chambers crawls with flesh seeking wire tendrils looking to merge with any living tissue and subsume it into the whole.</p><p><strong>Every turn roll 1d10.</strong> On 1-5 the location rolled is flooded with the tendrils, knocking everyone to the floor and forcing an Infection Check. On a Critical Failure character begins to merge with Caliban. 1d5 rounds, requires a Strength Check to be pulled free.</p><h3>Locations</h3><p><strong>1. FLOODED ATRIUM.</strong> The Jealousy of Caliban dominates the room, slumped over in a corner, half sunken in a pool of dark blood. It attacks anyone who isn't Infected but otherwise ignores the crew.</p><p><strong>2. COLLAPSED VENTRICLE.</strong> Hundreds of terminal monitors merged grotesquely with the organic bulkhead. Each of them displays a hideous unblinking eye (Sanity Save or gain 1d5 Stress). On the wall bordering the Inner Chamber is a password protected (\"ARIEL\") Control Console which allows the user to spy on anyone in The Dream using the nearest terminal as a camera.</p><p><strong>3. ROTTING CHAMBER.</strong> A jungle of gnarled veins and cables sprouting from every inch of the walls to the center of the chamber where the <strong>Avatar of Caliban</strong> sits on a twisted, oily throne. The awful crown on his head throbs with each pulse from the tangled veins. Killing the Avatar and donning the crown grants the user total control over all of The Dream's systems. Sanity Save [-] to take the crown off, otherwise it is impossible to remove without killing the user.</p><p><strong>4. ATRIUM.</strong> An obscene torture chamber. 3d10 denizens of The Dream hang on rusty meathooks while fist-sized Cyberleeches [C:45 Infection Check W:1] slowly digest the bodies.</p><p><strong>5. INNER CHAMBER.</strong> A dark and towering hollow. Black granite floors. Quiet except for faint wheezing. Fused into the wall is <strong>Caliban</strong>, pathetic and mutilated. His human form is unrecognizable and he cannot speak, only rasp out machine-assisted breaths. A black child-sized box lays in front of him. Inside of it lies <strong>Ariel</strong>, Dr. Bancali's daughter. She should have died long ago from terminal cancer, but Caliban/Bancali's tireless efforts have kept her alive, though unaging, for 23 years. She dies if removed from the box. Caliban only exists to keep her living.</p>","format":1},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":-1}},{"_id":"APOFp018Cal2","name":"Caliban Stats","type":"text","title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"content":"<h2>Caliban & His Forms</h2><h3>Avatar of Caliban</h3><p><strong>COMBAT:</strong> 80 Tendril x2 2d10 DMG + Infection<br><strong>INSTINCT:</strong> 65<br><strong>WOUNDS:</strong> 5(50)</p><ul><li><strong>Awful Crown:</strong> Can command any machine to do wearer's bidding. Characters with cybermods/slickware and androids get Sanity Saves to resist.</li></ul><p>Seven feet tall. Naked but covered in wires. Caliban's primary form when interacting physically with denizens of The Dream. His crown drags several meters of wire behind it like a train.</p><h3>Jealousy of Caliban</h3><p><strong>COMBAT:</strong> 80 Bash 5d10 DMG or Fleshcannon 3d10 DMG<br><strong>INSTINCT:</strong> 20<br><strong>WOUNDS:</strong> 5(45)</p><ul><li><strong>Fleshcannon:</strong> Shoots disgorged limbs, viscera, and blood at target. Infection Check [-].</li></ul><p>A grossly enlarged former human, swollen with fat, metal plates and tubes fused into its flesh.</p><h3>Caliban (Formerly Dr. Bancali)</h3><p><strong>COMBAT:</strong> 50<br><strong>INSTINCT:</strong> 85<br><strong>WOUNDS:</strong> 2(200)</p><ul><li><strong>Reinforcements:</strong> Caliban himself cannot fight, though he can call Chokespawn, Husks, or attempt to compel Infected Level 6+ to do his bidding (Sanity Save to resist). Reinforcements arrive within 1d10 rounds.</li><li><strong>Hard to Kill:</strong> Caliban is more of a loose hive mind at this point rather than a person, and makes a great campaign-length villain.</li><li>If the entire Dream is destroyed, there is a 10% chance Caliban escaped on some other Infected person or machine. If his original form in the Inner Chamber is killed, Prospero's Dream starts to fall apart. It will self destruct in 1d10 hours. Congratulations. You won.</li></ul>","format":1},"sort":1,"ownership":{"default":-1}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
